<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of the Two Sicilies</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1816–1861</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of the Two Sicilies was the largest state of pre-unification <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, formed in 1816 when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> king Ferdinand I merged the kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>. It covered the southern mainland and Sicily, with Naples as its capital. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Giuseppe Garibaldi</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/expedition-of-the-thousand">Expedition of the Thousand</a> overthrew it in 1860, and it was annexed to the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> in 1861.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-two-sicilies.jpg" alt="Kingdom of the Two Sicilies" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Flopao Derivative work: ZuppaDiCarlo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_the_Two_Sicilies_(1816)_(Sodacan_style).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
